To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Quantum disk upgrade SUMMARY
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076335021707

We noted that a recent doubling of memory without adding swap space had 
been unsuccessful and asked how disklabel and newfs are used to obtain a 
1gb swap space and the rest of the disk as a second partition on a new 
Quantum Atlas 4.2gb.

Thanks to Bruce Whittaker, Martyn Brown, Alan@nabeth.. and Alan Oborne 
for their replies.

a) Use disklabel to get characteristics
b) Use disklabel -e to edit these characteristics to what you require
c) Do not, under any circumstances, put the swap space as the first 
partition because swapping will overwrite the partition information.

