My original question is 

I installed RIS and DMU on an Alpha system running DU4.0.  The problem is
I don't know the boot command to boot a client either using RIS or DMU.

If I use the command 'boot ewa0', the DMU server takes over.  Then is there
a boot command to let the client machine boot up using RIS server?


Many thanks to Dave Parker <djp@unx.dec.com>.  Here is his answer.

You cannot have a client registered simultaneously to a RIS and DMU server nor 
to two RIS or two DMU servers.  The client makes a BOOTP request to perform a 
network boot and both RIS and DMU use BOOTP.  There is no way to indicate which 
service or server you really want.

