From tru64-unix-managers  Mon Jul 22 21:59:07 1996
From: Jerry Winegarden <jbw () oit ! duke ! edu>
Date: Mon, 22 Jul 1996 21:59:07 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: disktab entry for Micropolis 4421-07 needed
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076335021585


The answer is simple:   under OSF (nee DU), you don't need one.

Use /sbin/disklabel and it will create it's own!!!!

Specifically, use the following command:

/sbin/disklabel -rw rz# Micropolis4421

where # is the SCSI ID number of your drive (you may need to do a MAKEDEV rz#
first) (e.g. rz1)  

	and where the label Micropolis4421 is what ever you want it to be!

You can always check to see the labelling info on a drive by typing:

disklabel -r rz1  (or whatever your drive).  If there is labeling info there,
	it will display it, along with the partitioning info.
	(just like chpt -q for us old unix folks...:-)

If you need to "unlabel it" before you "relabel it", then try:

disklabel -z rz1 (or whatever your drive is)


(I knew to use disklabel to actually format the drive, but I thought you
needed a pointer into a disktab entry.  The man page on disklabel doesn't
make that very clear!)

Thanks to Jason Heyd, jheyd@lycos.com  for his extremely prompt and correct
answer!

