X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076335021552


Hi, I've been trying to obtain some insight into UBC (among other) related 
performance in Digital UNIX, specifically the UBC hit rate.  It would appear 
from the numerous discussons in osf managers archives that the "VmUBC" is by far 
the most useful in this realm.

The questions I have is as follows:

VmUBC shows hits and misses for the UFS/UBC as obtained from the namelist symbol 
"ufs_getapage_stats".  I believe this to be the "BSD buffer cache" information, 
not the "real" unified buffer cache statistics.

1)  Is anyone aware of a symbol which would provide the unified buffer cache
