Thanks to Mathias Koerber, Chander Ganevan and Todd Acheson. They all 
suggested to edit the sendmail.cf and increase the load average that I 
want sendmail to start rejecting connections.

Here's the mail from Chander Genevan:
	 sendmail will start rejecting connections once the load average
gets above a certain amount, but that is a user-configurable option.  You
might look into it...  The option is 'X' so you would need to look for a
line starting with 'OX<##>' where '<##>' is the load average that you want
sendmail to start rejecting connections at (select something arbitrarily
high, like: 

OX99

	and it should take care of the problem) .


Regards,
Armand

